1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galtung_(noble_family)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Google Translation of the Norwegian
2 CONT ===============================
2 CONT Married about 1610 with Elisabet Ottesdotter Orning. Unknown how many children they had, but three are mentioned in Strandbarm Boka
2 CONT
2 CONT It was Laurits who again did Torsnes a vikelig lands. He was a good and smart business man, who made money on lumber trade around 1620 - 1660, and put money in farm properties. The farms were generally easy to obtain at this time 
2 CONC when so many farmers had to walk from their farm because of harsh taxes. Elizabeth was also a good housekeeper, and had with her land as inheritance. When Lauritsalan died, he owned 53 farms or parts of farms totaling 70 Lauper bu
2 CONC tter. This corresponds to approximately 3/4 of the country of Strandebarm, farms are spread over Hardanger Sunnhordaland and Voss. Farm properties were split  between the children, Trolif 7 pieces: one son and six daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT (1 LAUP butter = 18kg butter) <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> RESIDENCE: 1636, Godseier at Torsnes
2 CONT
2 CONT OCCUPATION: Fogd over Halsnøy Abbey and Hardanger len, HO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH: 1587, (Galtung) to Torsnes, Jondal, HO
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: April 24, 1659, Torsnes, Jondal, Hardanger, HO
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIAL: Jondal Church, Hardanger, HO
2 CONT
2 CONT EVENT: 1621 Sentenced leiermål with 'Mergrete Styuersdaater'
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------- Family farm Torsnes [edit source]
2 CONT
2 CONT One consumption on Torsnes
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo: Elin Galtung Lihaug
2 CONT
2 CONT The farm Torsnes have remained within the same family from the 1100s until today. Mid 1600s landowner at Torsnes, Lauritz Johansson Galte, one of the largest landowners in Hardanger. Tax census in 1647 shows that he in addition to
2 CONC  Torsnes had 31 farms or farm parties in Hardanger, 13 in Sunnhordland and 6 in Voss. His son, Lauritz Galtung, was admiral in the Danish-Norwegian fleet and later feudal lord over Lister County and stayed low on Torsnes as an adu
2 CONC lt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauritz Johansson Galte owned the whole Torsnes in 1636 and then had built a new farmhouse after the fire in 1626. The new was listed by rough lumber and had two floors, each with its gallery on the south side, the top in the whol
2 CONC e building length, the bottom probably separated into two parts, one on each side of the "gateway". On the second floor there was a greater "herresal" but otherwise the rooms appear to have been relatively small
2 CONT hahä Definitions of ha exclamation used to express surprise, suspicion, triumph, or some other emotion. "Agreeing that from time to time we need a bit of help from outside, we ask for the occasional ‘ah hah !’" abbreviation hectar
2 CONC e(s). See also Ha!, HA Google Translate for Business:Translator ToolkitWebsite TranslatorGlobal Market Finder Turn off instant translationAbout Google TranslateMobileCommunityPrivacy & TermsHelpSend feedback
2 CONT
