1 OCCU Farmer, Admiral og lensherre, Admiral, adlet 1648. Admiral og vefalingsmann over Listerlen, Admiral i den Dansk/Norske Marine, Kaptajn i den dansk-norske flåde
1 TITL Admiral
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauritz Galtung was born at the family farm of Torsnes in Hardanger. He is the first in the family to have been called the younger Galtung-family, as he used Galtung rather than the earlier Galte. His father, Lauritz Johannessen G
2 CONC alte, was one of the biggest landowners in Hardanger. The tax-census of 1647 shows that he owned 32 farms or farmparts in Hardanger, 13 in Sunnhordaland, and 6 in Voss.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He was first married to Danish noblewoman Clara Gere of Bjørnstrup; however she died in 1647, only a few months after the marriage. In 1650 he got married again, to another Danish noblewoman, Barbara Grabow. Barbara and Lauritz ev
2 CONC entually got six children, the first four born in Bjørnstrup, Scania, and the last two born at Huseby, Farsund after moving to Norway in 1658 (as a result of the Danish loss of Scania by the terms of the Treaty of Roskilde).
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Literature
2 CONT
2 CONT H. D. Lind. Kong Frederik den Tredjes Sømagt. Det dansk–norske Søværns Historie 1648–1670. I Den Milo’ske Boghandel, Odense, 1896.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Ellertsen Galtung. Galtungslekten i fortid og nutid. Eget forlag, Oslo, 1974.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elin Galtung Lihaug. «Grabow, Galtung — og Pusjkin; Søkelys på en europeisk slektssammenheng». Norsk Slektshistorisk Tidsskrift, 39, 93–133, 2003.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elin Galtung Lihaug. «Aus Brandenburg nach Skandinavien, dem Baltikum und Rußland. Eine Abstammungslinie von Claus von Grabow bis Alexander Sergejewitsch Puschkin 1581–1837». Archiv für Familiengeschichtsforschung, 11, 32–46, 2007
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Han av den gamalnorske adelsætta Galtung frå Hardanger. Fekk fornye adelsbrevet sitt i 1648.
2 CONT
